  "notes": [
    {
      "noteType": "progress",
      "author": "Dr. Smith",
      "authorRole": "PCP",
      "content": "Patient presents for routine follow-up of HTN, T2DM, and hyperlipidemia. Reports good medication compliance but admits to missing evening Metformin doses 2-3x/week. Diet has been inconsistent — eating out frequently due to work schedule. Back pain is manageable with ibuprofen PRN.\n\nVitals: BP 142/88, HR 76, Wt 198 lbs (BMI 31.2)\n\nAssessment:\n1. T2DM — A1c 7.8%, up from 7.2% six months ago. Need to improve adherence and diet.\n2. HTN — Suboptimally controlled. Consider titrating Lisinopril vs adding second agent.\n3. Hyperlipidemia — LDL 138, above goal of <100 for diabetic patient.\n4. Low back pain — stable, conservative management.\n\nPlan:\n1. Reinforce medication adherence, especially evening Metformin. Consider switching to Metformin XR once daily.\n2. Recheck BP in 2 weeks. If still elevated, add amlodipine 5mg.\n3. Increase atorvastatin to 80mg if LDL not at goal in 3 months.\n4. Referral to nutritionist for diabetes diet counseling.\n5. Continue ibuprofen PRN for back pain.\n6. Labs in 3 months: A1c, lipid panel, BMP.",
      "summary": "Routine follow-up. A1c up to 7.8%, BP 142/88. Medication adherence needs improvement. Plan to optimize BP and lipid control.",
